Rule 1 (matrix dtype must be float or complex to avoid invalid dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 10)
>>
Rule 2 (avoid float16 to prevent device-not-found on CPU-only setups)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 6
>>
Rule 3 (matrix must be at least 2-D and square in its last two dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (if batched, all batch dimensions must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 3] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 5 (name must be a valid string from the allowed set)
{v_2 : str} |= (v_2 = "none") ∨ (v_2 = "sum") ∨ (v_2 = "max") ∨ (v_2 = "min")
